DEFINITIONS

"The Software" means Skorp7 Engine: its programs, including the editor, its source code, shaders and documentation, and any part of them. It does not include the third-party libraries listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, which keep their own licences.

"Runtime Files" means the parts of the Software that Skorp7 provides for inclusion in games and apps, as Skorp7 names them in the Software's documentation, and that a game or app needs in order to run.

"Product" means one game or interactive app that includes Runtime Files. Each game or app counts as its own Product, and its editions, updates and expansions count as part of it.

"Budget" means the total spent on developing a Product, plus any money raised or received for it. Spending counts wages, contractors, outsourcing, assets and tools. Money received counts investment, publisher advances and grants. Marketing spent after the Product's release does not count. Unpaid work does not count.

"Indie Product" means a Product whose Budget has never been more than GBP 100,000. A Product whose Budget passes GBP 100,000 stops being an Indie Product from that moment, and stays that way.

"Gross Revenue" means the money that actually reaches you from a Product, including sales, in-app purchases, subscriptions and advertising revenue, after deducting VAT and other sales taxes, refunds, chargebacks, and the share kept by the store or platform that sells it (such as Steam, a console store or an app store).

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO, FREE OF CHARGE

1.1 Use the Software for any purpose, including commercial work.
1.2 Read, study and reverse engineer the Software.
1.3 Modify the Software for your own use.
1.4 Own what you make with it. Your scenes, models, projects, renders and other content are yours.
1.5 Include Runtime Files, modified or not, in your Product and distribute them as part of it, under the terms in section 3.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

2.1 Redistribute the Software, modified or not, other than Runtime Files inside a Product. This includes the editor, the Software on its own, and any copy of the Software, modified or not, offered to others as an engine or editor.
2.2 Sell, rent or sublicense the Software, other than Runtime Files inside a Product.
2.3 Remove this license or any copyright notice from the Software.

The only authorised way to obtain the Software is from Skorp7, through Skorp7 Launcher or another source Skorp7 names.

3. ROYALTY

3.1 No royalty is due on an Indie Product.
3.2 For each Product that is not an Indie Product, you pay Skorp7 2.8% of its Gross Revenue above the first GBP 500,000 of Gross Revenue that Product has earned in total. The first GBP 500,000 of each Product is royalty-free. Only Gross Revenue earned after the Product stopped being an Indie Product is charged.
3.3 No royalty is due on anything other than a Product. This includes films, videos, renders, images, models and other assets made with the Software, internal tools that are not sold, and services such as consulting or visualisation work.
3.4 Nothing needs to be reported for an Indie Product, or until a Product's total Gross Revenue passes GBP 500,000. After that, for each calendar quarter, you send Skorp7 a report of that Product's Gross Revenue within 45 days of the quarter's end, and pay the royalty in GBP within 30 days of Skorp7's invoice.
3.5 Skorp7 may check your figures for a Product at most once a year, with 30 days' written notice. Skorp7 pays for the check, unless it finds that you underpaid by more than 5%, in which case you pay for it, as well as the amount underpaid.
3.6 If a payment for a Product is more than 60 days late after Skorp7 has given you written notice, your rights under this license for that Product end.
3.7 A later version of this license may not raise the royalty rate, lower the royalty-free amount or lower the Budget limit for a Product released while you held this version.
3.8 You do not have to show a splash screen, logo or "made with" credit.

4. GENERAL

Anything not granted here needs written permission from Skorp7. If you break these terms, other than as section 3.6 sets out, your rights under this license end.

